l, quarterly and semi-annual disclosure packages, including notes and relevant referenced material. U1, U3. | Define the source inventory, coverage units, cross-reference closure and disposition rules. A worked filing package must account for retained, structured, duplicated and unresolved content without treating page extraction as semantic completion. | Specified procedure; acquired-file inventory checked. Ch. 2 Apple and Ch. 3 coverage; `cases/apple/manifest.json` accounts for 121 annual pages, 13 annual notes and 10 interim notes. External incorporated documents and full semantic translation remain incomplete. G5, G11. The added source corpus now has 192 checked annual/interim files across nine issuers and 2018–2025; incorporated-package closure and semantic annotation remain open. |\n57:| MC03 | Represent narrative policies, qualifications, commitments and cross-references, including material that is not executable yet. U1, U3, D. | Specify narrative assertion types, modality/quantifiers, links to affected amounts and obligations, and reviewed translation into constraints without inventing thresholds. | Specified Narrative/coverage records and modality rules in Ch. 3 and Core 0. Apple note and cross-reference obligations are retained; representative debt language is interpreted. Complete translation of all material narratives remains open. G2, G11. |\n59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\n80:| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\n102:| MC28 | Connect the full design through complete synthetic and real disclosure cases. U1, U2, U3, D. | Supply a known-history synthetic company and a named annual/interim real package across multiple dates; trace representative notes through records, constraints, alternatives and all affected future statements. Add structural finance/sector cases before fixing the core types. | Reference cases delivered in Ch. 2: complete synthetic Northstar history/revision/forecast and named Apple annual/interim inventory, notes and conditional stress. Ch. 9 supplies sector/finance structures. Real-company full semantic closure and independent case annotation remain open; no complete Apple forecast is claimed. G4, G5, G7. Nine eight-year report sequences are now source-checked; report-wide semantic cases and executable oracles remain to be prepared. |\n140:plan; v1 evidence remains preserved. This advances MC01, MC03, MC05, MC19–22,\n141:MC28, MC30 and MC33–35 without closing semantic, accounting or forecast\nAGENTS.md\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/AGENTS.md\ndocs/design/review/pre-repair-2026-10-02/AGE